# Verifiable Learning Sources

Agents **must not invent** pedagogical facts, fingerings, grammar rules, CEFR mappings, tempos, pass criteria, definitions, or exercise instructions. Every **learning item** shown to the user needs an **online, checkable source**.

## What counts as a learning item

Anything the user is taught or asked to practice:

- Piano: scale fingerings, tempos, lesson steps, pass rules, mode/key facts
- English path: unit scope, grammar explanations, frame patterns, placement rubrics, CEFR band claims
- Vocabulary: definitions, usage notes, mnemonics, example sentences (when curated in seed/catalog)

User-generated content (saved words, YouTube notes they pasted) is exempt. **Agent-authored curriculum is not.**

## Required source shape

Store sources in code as `LearningSource` (`src/lib/learning-source.ts`):

```typescript
{
  title: string;       // e.g. "pianoscales.org — B major"
  url: string;         // https://… public URL the user can open
  note?: string;       // what this source backs (fingerings, tempo, etc.)
}
```

- **`url` must be a real https link** — not "RCM", "standard pedagogy", or "common knowledge".
- **Verify before shipping**: open/search the URL (or equivalent official doc) and confirm the claim matches.
- **Tests must not be the source of truth** — never assert agent-invented facts without an external reference in the same PR.

## Forbidden

- Heuristic rules ("5-sharp keys start on 2") without a chart citation
- Comments like `RCM-style` with no RCM URL
- Duplicating wrong data into tests to make CI pass
- LLM-generated lesson bodies saved as curriculum without a cited syllabus/link

## Where this applies

| Area | Typical files |
| :--- | :------------ |
| Piano curriculum | `src/features/piano/curriculum/**`, `lesson-detail.ts`, `seed.ts` |
| English path | `src/features/path/curriculum/**`, `placement/**`, path catalog copy that teaches |
| Shared | `src/lib/learning-source.ts` |

## Agent duties

| Agent | Duty |
| :---- | :--- |
| **Director** | Every curriculum task lists required sources or "reuse existing cited source". Block plans that invent facts. |
| **Implementer** | Add/update `sources` on learning items; fetch and verify URLs; add tests that check source URLs exist, not invented fingerings. |
| **Security Reviewer** | Reject curriculum changes with missing URLs, broken links, or claims that don't match the cited page. |

## When no public URL exists

Stop and ask the user for an official PDF, book edition, or link — **do not guess**. Temporary user-supplied text (YouTube note) may be tagged `source: user` and is not agent authority.

## Ask AI (exercise help)

When adding AI explainers on exercises:

- **Server builds the reference pack** from the current lesson + sources + glossary — never trust client-sent lesson text.
- System prompt must forbid facts outside the pack (`grounded-ask-ai.ts`).
- Temperature **0**; filter `citedSourceTitles` to the allowlist only.
- Mock mode must still refuse to invent facts outside the pack.
